@startuml
title Activity Diagram: UC-03 Manage Products

|Customer|
start
:[Step 1.0] Customer selects "Products"\non the Home Page;

|System|
:[Step 1.1] Retrieve and display the\ncurrent product catalog;

|Customer|
:[Step 2.0] Select a specific product\nto view its full details;

|System|
:[Step 2.1] Display product details (price breakdown,\nsize options, ingredients, allergen info);

if (Customer wants to customize the selected product?) then (Yes)
  :Start Manage Cake Design use case;
else (No)
  :Continue browsing the catalog;
endif

|Staff/Admin|
:[Step 3.0] Select "Manage Products"\nfrom the Admin Panel Dashboard;

|System|
:[Step 3.1] Display the Manage Products page\nwith all current products;

|Staff/Admin|
:[Step 4.0] Choose Add New Product, or select\nan existing product to edit or remove;

|System|
:[Step 4.1] Display blank form for add,\nor pre-filled form for edit;

|Staff/Admin|
:[Step 5.0] Enter or update the product details\nand click Save or confirm Remove;

|System|
:[Step 5.1] Validate required fields and formatting;

if (Information valid and complete?) then (Yes)
  if (Product update conflicts with an active order?) then (Yes)
    :[Exc 5.2.1] Warn Staff/Admin\nbefore saving change;
    if (Staff/Admin confirms save?) then (Yes)
      :[Step 5.2] Save the product record;
    else (No)
      :Cancel the update;
    endif
  else (No)
    :[Step 5.2] Save the product record to the database;
  endif
  
  :[Step 5.2] Refresh the live catalog;
  :[Step 5.3] Display confirmation message;
else (No)
  :[Exc 5.1.1] Prompt for missing or\ncorrected fields;
  :[Exc 5.1.1] Do not save the record;
endif

|System|
stop
@enduml
